"""Generate a standalone, peak-preserving Phase 5 spectral inspector."""
import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];d=root/'Docs/Phase5'
raw={}
for r in csv.DictReader((d/'spectra.csv').open()):
 key=f"{r['mode']}/{r['requested_hz']}/{r['hq']}"
 raw.setdefault(key,[]).append([float(r['hz']),float(r['amplitude_db'])])
# Keep the strongest bin in each eight-bin group; full CSV remains unthinned.
spectra={k:[max(v[i:i+8],key=lambda p:p[1]) for i in range(0,len(v),8)] for k,v in raw.items()}
alias=list(csv.DictReader((d/'aliasing.csv').open()))
html='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>DISRUPTION Phase 5 HQ spectra</title><style>body{background:#101213;color:#ddd;font:16px system-ui;max-width:1120px;margin:35px auto}select{padding:9px;background:#242729;color:#eee}svg{background:#1b1e20;width:100%}path{fill:none;stroke-width:1.3}text{fill:#aaa;font:13px system-ui}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:7px 20px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #444}</style><h1>DISRUPTION · HQ analysis</h1><p>Measured C++ output. 4× linear-phase FIR nonlinear processing; both digital CRUSH stages remain native. Drive36/Damage100. The spectra use coherent sine bins at approximately 5/10/15 kHz and 48 kHz host rate.</p><select id="mode"><option value="0">BURN</option><option value="1">BREAK</option><option value="2">RIP</option><option value="3">CRUSH</option><option value="4">CHAOS</option></select> <select id="frequency"><option>5000</option><option>10000</option><option>15000</option></select><p><span style="color:#ff6d3b">HQ OFF</span> · <span style="color:#45c5df">HQ ON</span></p><svg id="plot" viewBox="0 0 1080 450"></svg><table id="table"></table><p>Frequency axis 0–24 kHz, vertical −120 to +6 dBFS. Plot groups eight bins using their strongest bin so narrow coherent peaks remain visible; spectra.csv contains every measured bin. Analysis excludes DC and all below-Nyquist integer harmonics of the actual source bin. Aliases coinciding with legitimate harmonic bins cannot be separated by this method. No subjective listening approval is implied.</p><script>const spectra=SPECTRA,alias=ALIAS;function draw(){let m=document.querySelector('#mode').value,f=document.querySelector('#frequency').value,svg=document.querySelector('#plot');let out='<path stroke="#555" d="M60 20V410H1050"/>';for(let db=-120;db<=0;db+=20){let y=25+(6-db)*3;out+=`<path stroke="#303638" d="M60 ${y}H1050"/><text x="5" y="${y+4}">${db} dB</text>`;}for(let hz=0;hz<=24000;hz+=4000){let x=60+990*hz/24000;out+=`<text x="${x-12}" y="435">${hz/1000}k</text>`;}[0,1].forEach(hq=>{let rows=spectra[`${m}/${f}/${hq}`]||[],path=rows.map((p,i)=>`${i?'L':'M'}${60+990*p[0]/24000},${25+(6-Math.max(-120,Math.min(6,p[1])))*3}`).join(' ');out+=`<path stroke="${hq?'#45c5df':'#ff6d3b'}" d="${path}"/>`;});svg.innerHTML=out;let r=alias.filter(x=>x.rate==='48000'&&x.mode===m&&x.requested_hz===f),table='<tr><th>HQ</th><th>Actual input Hz</th><th>Non-harmonic RMS</th><th>Total RMS</th><th>Alias / total dB</th></tr>';r.forEach(x=>table+=`<tr><td>${+x.hq?'ON':'OFF'}</td><td>${x.actual_hz}</td><td>${x.alias_rms}</td><td>${x.total_rms}</td><td>${x.alias_to_total_db}</td></tr>`);document.querySelector('#table').innerHTML=table;let names=['BURN','BREAK','RIP','CRUSH','CHAOS'];document.querySelector('#audio').src=names[+m]+(document.querySelector('#stack').checked?'-Stack':'-Engine')+'-OFF-then-ON.wav';}document.querySelectorAll('select').forEach(x=>x.onchange=draw);document.querySelector('#stack').onchange=draw;draw();</script>'''.replace('SPECTRA',json.dumps(spectra)).replace('ALIAS',json.dumps(alias))
(d/'HQ-Spectral-Inspector.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8');print(d/'HQ-Spectral-Inspector.html')
